1. Introduction
Your privacy is extremely important to us. This Privacy Policy explains how data is handled when you play The Last Stand on the Meta Horizon platform.

2. Data Collection
We do not collect, store, or log any personal information or gameplay data.
Everything you do in the Application stays locally on your device. Specifically, we do not collect:
Personal identifiers (such as your name, email, or Meta Horizon profile ID).
Device identifiers, IP addresses, or hardware performance logs.
In-game actions, scores, or achievements.
Location, voice, or spatial environment data.
Note: Meta may collect standard telemetry, crash reports, and anonymized aggregate usage data as part of its own platform policies. Please refer to the Supplemental Meta Platforms Technologies Privacy Policy to learn more about Meta's data practices.

3. Data Processing & Third Parties
Because we do not collect any user data, we do not process, share, or sell any information. We do not integrate third-party analytics trackers (such as Google Analytics) or advertising networks.

4. Data Deletion
Since we do not collect or store any of your personal data or user activity, there is nothing for us to store and nothing for us to delete. If you wish to delete data associated with your Meta account, you must manage your Meta Quest privacy settings directly through your Meta headset or account portal.
5. Children’s Privacy
The Application does not intentionally collect information from anyone, including children. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child is using this Application, please monitor their device usage or contact Meta. 

6. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our Application. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page.

